# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Captured test fixtures are BYTES, not source — MONEY-1198
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Every fixture under a `__tests__/fixtures/` tree is a verbatim capture of what
# an exchange, AMC or API actually served. Their VALUE is that they are
# byte-identical to the real response, because the defects they pin are invisible
# in anything hand-written or re-serialised: doubled double-quotes in a title
# row, trailing spaces in header cells, a `.xls` extension over OOXML bytes, the
# "Lakhs"/"Lacs" split, a reversed "Rating / Industry" header.
#
# Prettier reformatting one silently destroys that property. It already happened:
# `prettier --write` (via lint-staged's `*.{json,css,scss,md}` rule) pretty-
# printed `amc-pages/mirae-downloads-error.json`, turning `"ReturnCode":"9999"`
# into `"ReturnCode": "9999"` — which broke the test asserting on the raw error
# body, AFTER the commit had been verified green. A fixture that has been
# formatted is no longer evidence of anything.
#
# The same reasoning is already written into the MONEY-1186 fixture commit:
# reducing an XLSX means rebuilding its zip, and the rebuild would quietly
# normalise the very defects the tests exist to pin. This makes that rule
# mechanical instead of hoping nobody stages a fixture.
